# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LSEAT Engineering Portal
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in the value.
#   cp .env.example .env
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY
#
# Web3Forms ACCESS KEY, obtained from https://web3forms.com
# (Dashboard > Access Keys > "Add Access Key").
#
# This is a PUBLIC client-side key: it is intentionally prefixed with PUBLIC_
# so that Astro exposes it to the browser bundle (import.meta.env.PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY).
# It is not a secret and cannot be kept server-side, because the contact form
# submits directly from the browser to https://api.web3forms.com/submit.
#
# Destination mailbox: contact@lseat.eu
#   All submissions delivered with this key are routed to contact@lseat.eu.
#   Change the destination in the Web3Forms dashboard if this ever diverges.
#
# Anti-spam: the form ships with a honeypot field ("botcheck") that silently
# aborts bot submissions. Google reCAPTCHA v3 can additionally be enabled from
# the Web3Forms dashboard (ReCAPTCHA tab) and works with the same access key.
#
# Without a valid key the form refuses to submit and points the visitor to
# contact@lseat.eu.
PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=your_web3forms_access_key_here